      "text": [
        ":\nكَتَبْتُ إِلَيْهِ أَسْأَلُهُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ تَمَتَّعَ بِامْرَأَةٍ ثُمَّ وَهَبَ لَهَا أَيَّامَهَا قَبْلَ أَنْ يُفْضِيَ إِلَيْهَا أَوْ وَهَبَ لَهَا أَيَّامَهَا بَعْدَ مَا أَفْضَى إِلَيْهَا هَلْ لَهُ أَنْ يَرْجِعَ فِيمَا وَهَبَ لَهَا مِنْ ذَلِكَ فَوَقَّعَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ \"لاَ يَرْجِعُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4590 - Ali bin Ri'ab narrated:\nHe wrote to Imam (as) asking about a man who engaged in Mutah (temporary marriage) with a woman and then gifted her the remaining days of the contract before consummating the marriage or after consummating it.\nHe asked whether the man could revoke what he had gifted her from those days.\nThe Imam (as) replied: \"He cannot take it back.\""
        ]
      }
    },
